<p>Fixed some minor grammatical stuff and localization issues per te.</p>
<p>As for the article&#8230;ehhhh, I'm not really sold on this &quot;revenge on the teachers&quot; thing as a concept, but even if I was, the execution is kind of bogged down here.</p>
<p>For starters, I know it shows up in other articles, but I don't care for the repeatedly struck through object classes. Seems to me that changes in classification would be covered in the note that you included later in the article. From an aesthetic standpoint, I find it displeasing. The containment drags a bit, making it feel like I've had to slog before I've even gotten to the skip, which has the effect, in my opinion, of burying your lede.</p>
<p>The sphere-thing being put into the teacher along with a note&#8230;I dunno. It's not egregious, but it seems a tad over the top in terms of inserting scary imagery. It also further cements in my mind a kind of silly image of the creator of this phenomenon. You've got someone or something sophisticated enough to make anti-grav mind-warping orbs and perfrom complex human surgery, but its stated goal is &quot;school sucks maaaan&quot;. Kind of a disconnect for me.</p>
<p>Finally, speaking as someone who got skewered recently for even hinting at a complicated decomm attempt, the very end of the article strikes me as unnecessarily distracting from your skip.</p>

							</div>

								
